{"id":"twitter:1685836239105126401","tweet_id":"1685836239105126401","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685836239105126401","title":"@UAArtisansRock It is time for Defense Production Act to kick in. We can't have someone cutting off operational coverage while simultaneously allowing","summary":"@UAArtisansRock It is time for Defense Production Act to kick in. We can't have someone cutting off operational coverage while simultaneously allowing monetizing of Russian disinfo You learn quickly the Department of Defense does not like playing FAFO with contractors. This is twice. DPA now","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T02:14:15+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/i/status/1685832798219960320","reply_tweet_id":"1685832798219960320","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@UAArtisansRock It is time for Defense Production Act to kick in.<br><br>We can&#x27;t have someone cutting off operational coverage while simultaneously allowing monetizing of Russian disinfo<br><br>You learn quickly the Department of Defense does not like playing FAFO with contractors.<br><br>This is twice. DPA now</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685836239105126401","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 02:14 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1685832715910656000","tweet_id":"1685832715910656000","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685832715910656000","title":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole What? What is from the Old English hwæt, used to refer to nouns, usually things, in abstraction Derive","summary":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole What? What is from the Old English hwæt, used to refer to nouns, usually things, in abstraction Derived from the Old High German hwaz, its root is from PIE word *kwod, which is the neutered singular of *kwos \"who,\" All of these from PIE root *kwo- (like knowledge)","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T02:00:15+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/RDeckard_2049/status/1685831779289333761","reply_tweet_id":"1685831779289333761","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole What?<br><br>What is from the Old English hwæt, used to refer to nouns, usually things, in abstraction<br><br>Derived from the Old High German hwaz, its root is from PIE  word *kwod, which is the neutered singular of *kwos &quot;who,&quot; <br><br>All of these from PIE root *kwo- (like knowledge)</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685832715910656000","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 02:00 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1685831872352325632","tweet_id":"1685831872352325632","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685831872352325632","title":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, \"How do you know what Putin said?\" So I quoted Putin It does not make sense because it is a","summary":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, \"How do you know what Putin said?\" So I quoted Putin It does not make sense because it is all nonsense If Russia speaks, Russia lies. You never know truth until Russia denies.","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T01:56:54+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/RDeckard_2049/status/1685828033348096000","reply_tweet_id":"1685828033348096000","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, &quot;How do you know what Putin said?&quot;<br><br>So I quoted Putin<br><br>It does not make sense because it is all nonsense<br><br>If Russia speaks, Russia lies. You never know  truth until Russia denies.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685831872352325632","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 01:56 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1685831350694092802","tweet_id":"1685831350694092802","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685831350694092802","title":"@AngryOniOn7 @SLAV_Tchazzar @zhurov101 @AngrierPotato2 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestToma","summary":"@AngryOniOn7 @SLAV_Tchazzar @zhurov101 @AngrierPotato2 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestTomato @TheReportinator @ChadDBedson @PaulDBedson @Bellingdawg @Bellingdog2 @ReportinatorClb @Reportinat0r @georgegalloway @MoatsTV @RabbiUkraine Malofeev is good example of corruption in Russia He used his billion","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T01:54:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/ArchaeologyX/status/1685813224359264256","reply_tweet_id":"1685813224359264256","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@AngryOniOn7 @SLAV_Tchazzar @zhurov101 @AngrierPotato2 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestTomato @TheReportinator @ChadDBedson @PaulDBedson @Bellingdawg @Bellingdog2 @ReportinatorClb @Reportinat0r @georgegalloway @MoatsTV @RabbiUkraine Malofeev is good example of corruption in Russia<br><br>He used his billions to fund neonazi movements all over the world AND he bankrolled much of the fake &quot;separatist war&quot;<br><br>Malofeev was given Tsargard TV as a reward. He tried to hire his Fox News MAGA buddy John Hanick to run it <a href=\"https://t.co/MhH5uiEK9z\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/MhH5uiEK9z</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/add054e255680c4bfac90ee5e88cc66a.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685831350694092802","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 01:54 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/add054e255680c4bfac90ee5e88cc66a.jpg"]}
{"id":"twitter:1685830722475425792","tweet_id":"1685830722475425792","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685830722475425792","title":"@zhurov101 @SLAV_Tchazzar @AngrierPotato2 @AngryOniOn7 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestToma","summary":"@zhurov101 @SLAV_Tchazzar @AngrierPotato2 @AngryOniOn7 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestTomato @TheReportinator @ChadDBedson @PaulDBedson @Bellingdawg @Bellingdog2 @ReportinatorClb @Reportinat0r @georgegalloway @MoatsTV @RabbiUkraine In a weird way corruption in Russia is more a service to the enemies","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T01:52:20+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/i/status/1685812560052756481","reply_tweet_id":"1685812560052756481","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@zhurov101 @SLAV_Tchazzar @AngrierPotato2 @AngryOniOn7 @Ostblock_Latina @russophobic_p @Alephi_01 @PeteeM3 @RodgerNorman4 @FrankTrenton1 @AngriestTomato @TheReportinator @ChadDBedson @PaulDBedson @Bellingdawg @Bellingdog2 @ReportinatorClb @Reportinat0r @georgegalloway @MoatsTV @RabbiUkraine In a weird way corruption in Russia is more a service to the enemies of Russia.<br><br>I mean why does Shoigu have a 20,000,000 mansion? <a href=\"https://t.co/OOUh2OQrOQ\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/OOUh2OQrOQ</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/0e3a7afd8dca0251b10aaac50a67c2ae.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685830722475425792","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 01:52 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/0e3a7afd8dca0251b10aaac50a67c2ae.jpg"]}
{"id":"twitter:1685829993241157632","tweet_id":"1685829993241157632","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1685829993241157632","title":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, \"What is this?\" I defined \"this\": This is a demonstrative pronoun and adjective derived fro","summary":"@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, \"What is this?\" I defined \"this\": This is a demonstrative pronoun and adjective derived from a North Germanic phrase of \"tha-si\" Tha came from the base of *þa (That) combined with old English versions of \"the. \" Originally there were over 15 versions of \"this\"","date":"2023-07-31","published":"2023-07-31T01:49:26+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/RDeckard_2049/status/1685828150864035840","reply_tweet_id":"1685828150864035840","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@RDeckard_2049 @Alexand34489248 @narrative_hole You asked, &quot;What is this?&quot;<br><br>I defined &quot;this&quot;:<br><br>This is a demonstrative pronoun and adjective derived from a North Germanic phrase of &quot;tha-si&quot;  Tha came from the base of *þa (That) combined with old English versions of &quot;the. &quot; Originally there were over 15 versions of &quot;this&quot;</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1685829993241157632","display_date":"July 31, 2023 · 01:49 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
