{"id":"twitter:1684624102017896448","tweet_id":"1684624102017896448","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1684624102017896448","title":"@leveuho_nafo @Xap89Xap891 @squatsons I'd balance a bit of Libertarian thinking with some Frankfurt School. One activity I like to do is the etymology","summary":"@leveuho_nafo @Xap89Xap891 @squatsons I'd balance a bit of Libertarian thinking with some Frankfurt School. One activity I like to do is the etymology of \"critical\" comparing from Kantian humanism, Frankfurt, and praxis al a Friere I also like Foucalt, Bakhtin, Kristeva, Deleuze and Guattari, Vygotsky, and Luria","date":"2023-07-27","published":"2023-07-27T17:57:39+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/i/status/1684616525242601472","reply_tweet_id":"1684616525242601472","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@leveuho_nafo @Xap89Xap891 @squatsons I&#x27;d balance a bit of Libertarian thinking with some Frankfurt School.<br><br>One activity I like to do is the etymology of &quot;critical&quot; comparing from Kantian humanism, Frankfurt, and praxis al a Friere <br><br>I also like Foucalt, Bakhtin, Kristeva, Deleuze and Guattari, Vygotsky, and Luria</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1684624102017896448","display_date":"July 27, 2023 · 17:57 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
