{"id":"twitter:1679120223968870400","tweet_id":"1679120223968870400","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1679120223968870400","title":"The word craic is back in my kids' middle school. In Red Sox territory (as Yankee Fans) so, really never left 100% youngins use an anglicized spelling","summary":"The word craic is back in my kids' middle school. In Red Sox territory (as Yankee Fans) so, really never left 100% youngins use an anglicized spelling of \"crack\" You sometimes hear a grey hair correct a kid, but I think language changes are based.","date":"2023-07-12","published":"2023-07-12T13:27:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>The word craic is back in my kids&#x27; middle school.<br>In Red Sox territory (as Yankee Fans) so, really never left 100%<br>youngins use an anglicized spelling of &quot;crack&quot;<br>You sometimes hear a grey hair correct a kid, but<br>I think language changes are based.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1679120223968870400","display_date":"July 12, 2023 · 13:27 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
