{"id":"twitter:1676337983845285889","tweet_id":"1676337983845285889","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1676337983845285889","title":"As night rises over our bay wind ripples in an umbrella bent, upturned; a clapper in a metal trash can drum wires on speckled green paint peeling in w","summary":"As night rises over our bay wind ripples in an umbrella bent, upturned; a clapper in a metal trash can drum wires on speckled green paint peeling in winds of forgotten memory so we walk by towards last light #smallpoems #mastoprompt","date":"2023-07-04","published":"2023-07-04T21:11:34+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":["smallpoems","mastoprompt"],"body_html":"<p>As night<br>rises over <br>our bay<br>wind ripples<br>in an umbrella<br>bent,<br>upturned;<br>a clapper<br> in a metal<br> trash can drum<br>wires on speckled<br>green paint peeling<br>in winds of<br>forgotten<br>memory<br>so we walk<br>by towards<br>last light<br>#smallpoems #mastoprompt</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1676337983845285889","display_date":"July 04, 2023 · 21:11 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
